# The owner's eyes-on 4-GPC 3-CRT session of 2026-09-22, replayed.
#
# Played into a RESTORED vehicle (g3-3crt-ops301-idp3): through the Manager
# or the control port ('play FILE'), or as synctest.sh's fourth argument.  A
# resume deliberately does not replay the script that built a configuration.
#
# RECONSTRUCTED, NOT RECORDED.  The IDP/CRT SEL movements and their times are
# exact, from panel.log (seconds after the panel started, shown in each
# comment).  The KEYS AND THEIR ORDER are exact, from the keyboard logs, and
# which CRT each reached is from the MEDS2 logs -- but the keyboard logs then
# carried no timestamps, so each key's moment is a guess placed inside the
# window the switch times allow (FAULT SUMM reached CRT3, so it falls while
# LEFT was on 3).  KB2's second RESUME reached no CRT's log; it is placed in
# the RIGHT=3 window, where it most plausibly went.  stsKeyboard.py now stamps
# its log, so a session flown after this can be replayed exactly.
#
# Everything the owner did was in the first 2.5 minutes; the run then sat
# idle for over 30.  It flew at 0.70 of real time while a headless restore of
# the same capture flies at 1.000 -- which is what this replay is for.

